I can get you one of those.


00:30:42.706 --> 00:30:46.005
Brand new, just like this.
I'll have it delivered.


00:30:46.410 --> 00:30:47.900
No, thank you.


00:30:57.621 --> 00:30:59.646
Hey. Where is that?


00:30:59.756 --> 00:31:01.587
Aspen. We just got back.


00:31:02.292 --> 00:31:03.953
Had a great time.
You know who we met?


00:31:04.061 --> 00:31:05.358
Who?


00:31:06.063 --> 00:31:07.553
Burt Reynolds.


00:31:07.965 --> 00:31:11.025
Yeah? Yeah?
Yeah. I'm not kidding.


00:31:11.802 --> 00:31:15.738
A lot people from Hollywood
go up there now. They're
buying up everything.


00:31:15.839 --> 00:31:17.466
This is your place?
Mmm.


00:31:17.608 --> 00:31:21.442
You know what that's worth?
Ski in, ski out.
Five bedrooms.


00:31:21.578 --> 00:31:24.274
Sauna. Everything.
We were guests.


00:31:29.419 --> 00:31:31.046
It's your place.


00:31:46.169 --> 00:31:48.660
Isn't there
something we can do,


00:31:50.507 --> 00:31:53.067
about leaving
the big guy alone?


00:31:53.477 --> 00:31:55.411
You know who I mean.


00:31:55.512 --> 00:31:59.073
I don't report what
you just said, I can
get in a lot of trouble.


00:31:59.182 --> 00:32:02.151
I do report it,
then the trouble is yours.


00:32:04.187 --> 00:32:06.485
I'm hoping you won't do that.


00:32:07.324 --> 00:32:09.849
Richie, come on.
I'm not taping it.


00:32:09.993 --> 00:32:12.826
How do you know?
Because we're friends.


00:32:13.163 --> 00:32:15.597
And I'm telling you,
this is a real offer.


00:32:15.699 --> 00:32:17.599
From who? Your uncle?


00:32:21.305 --> 00:32:23.796
Why would you do this?
Why would you risk
our friendship?


00:32:23.907 --> 00:32:25.272
Because


00:32:27.544 --> 00:32:29.842
I care what happens to you.


00:32:31.915 --> 00:32:33.780
You shouldn't have done this.


00:32:33.884 --> 00:32:36.944
I had to, I had no choice.
Neither do you. Richie!


00:32:37.821 --> 00:32:41.621
You don't have a choice.
Just leave Frank Lucas alone.


00:32:43.327 --> 00:32:44.760
Frank Lucas?


00:32:45.996 --> 00:32:47.122
Yeah.


00:32:49.800 --> 00:32:52.667
You tell Marie I had to leave.
I'm sorry.


00:32:53.503 --> 00:32:54.970
Tell her why.


00:33:37.881 --> 00:33:39.348
Don't shoot! Don't shoot! Talk! Talk!
Don't shoot!


00:33:39.449 --> 00:33:41.747
Are you Richie Roberts?
Yes, so what?


00:33:42.686 --> 00:33:44.517
You've been served. I'm sorry.


00:33:59.269 --> 00:34:00.258
WOMAN: All right.


00:34:04.274 --> 00:34:05.263
(WHISPERING) Laurie.


00:34:07.411 --> 00:34:11.108
Look, I'm sorry I never
gave you the kind of life
you wanted, all right.


00:34:11.248 --> 00:34:13.546
I'm sorry it was never enough.


00:34:16.653 --> 00:34:19.281
Don't punish me
for being honest.


00:34:19.423 --> 00:34:21.391
Don't take my boy away.


00:34:21.792 --> 00:34:23.089
(SCOFFS)


00:34:23.760 --> 00:34:27.093
What are you saying?
That because you were honest


00:34:27.230 --> 00:34:30.393
and you didn't take money
like every other cop,
I left you?


00:34:30.500 --> 00:34:33.025
No, you don't take money
for one reason.


00:34:33.136 --> 00:34:35.934
To buy being dishonest
about everything else.


00:34:36.440 --> 00:34:38.431
And that's worse
than taking money nobody
gives a shit about.


00:34:38.575 --> 00:34:41.544
Drug money, gambling money
nobody's gonna miss.


00:34:41.945 --> 00:34:45.403
You know,
I'd rather you took it
and been honest with me.


00:34:45.515 --> 00:34:48.211
Or don't take it.
I don't care. But then
don't go cheat on me.


00:34:48.318 --> 00:34:51.412
Don't cheat on your kid
by never being around.
Don't go out and get laid


00:34:51.521 --> 00:34:54.456
by your snitches
and your secretaries
and strippers!


00:34:54.591 --> 00:34:57.321
I can tell by just looking,
she's one of them.


00:34:57.461 --> 00:34:58.450
You...


00:34:58.762 --> 00:35:03.062
You think you're going
to heaven because
you're honest, but you're not.


00:35:03.467 --> 00:35:06.061
You're going to the same
hell as the crooked cops
you can't stand.


00:35:06.169 --> 00:35:07.227
(DOOR OPENING)


00:35:07.337 --> 00:35:08.895
BAILIFF: All rise.


00:35:13.310 --> 00:35:15.301
JUDGE: Please be seated.


00:35:16.480 --> 00:35:18.175
Miss Dickerson,


00:35:18.315 --> 00:35:20.806
before the court
renders its opinion,


00:35:20.951 --> 00:35:23.613
is there anything else
you'd like to be heard on?


00:35:23.720 --> 00:35:25.449
Yes, Your Honor.


00:35:25.555 --> 00:35:28.683
Your Honor, a lot has
been said here today
about how unsavory


00:35:28.825 --> 00:35:32.784
Mr. Roberts' environment
is for a child.
How dangerous it is.


00:35:32.896 --> 00:35:36.662
We tell him to protect us.
We give him that
responsibility,


00:35:36.800 --> 00:35:39.325
but then say, "Oh, we don't
trust you to raise a child.


00:35:39.469 --> 00:35:40.993
"We don't think
you're fit for that."


00:35:41.104 --> 00:35:42.696
I'm not.


00:35:43.507 --> 00:35:44.974
You're right.


00:35:46.176 --> 00:35:48.610
Being around me
is no place for a kid.


00:35:48.712 --> 00:35:51.943
You take him to Vegas.
I'll come see him when I can.


00:35:54.885 --> 00:35:58.514
Your Honor, I want
to apologize for wasting
the court's time.


00:36:10.400 --> 00:36:12.095
FRANK: Doc.


00:36:12.202 --> 00:36:13.601
I see them.


00:36:13.703 --> 00:36:15.193
DETECTIVE: There he is.


00:36:33.723 --> 00:36:35.350
The fuck is this guy doing?


00:36:36.126 --> 00:36:37.457
DOC: Hey!
Champagne.


00:36:37.561 --> 00:36:39.756
DOC: Merry Christmas,
Detectives.
For us?


00:36:39.863 --> 00:36:41.694
DOC: Yeah. Enjoy that.


00:36:42.065 --> 00:36:44.397
You fellas have a good time.
Mmm-hmm.


00:36:45.802 --> 00:36:47.360
It's Cristal.


00:36:51.208 --> 00:36:53.506
<i>MAN ON TV: South Vietnamese
troops called in air strikes</i>


00:36:53.610 --> 00:36:56.545
<i>on Communist positions
inside the city.</i>


00:36:58.048 --> 00:37:00.744
Paying off Johnny Law,
that's one thing.


00:37:00.851 --> 00:37:02.443
There ain't no problem
with that.


00:37:02.552 --> 00:37:05.248
I've been paying off
the police since I
was 10 years old.


00:37:05.355 --> 00:37:08.017
Put more of their kids
through college than
the National Merit Award.


00:37:08.158 --> 00:37:09.921
Give me one of
them round one... Yeah.


00:37:10.026 --> 00:37:11.960
This is different,
though. These...


00:37:12.062 --> 00:37:15.964
Special Investigative Unit.
That's their problem.
They think they're special.


00:37:16.066 --> 00:37:18.694
Fucking crooks.
No code of ethics.


00:37:18.835 --> 00:37:19.859
What do you think?


00:37:19.970 --> 00:37:22.097
Looks great. It's beautiful.


00:37:22.405 --> 00:37:23.531
Good.


00:37:24.140 --> 00:37:26.199
The police, that ain't
the only somebody
I'm worried about.


00:37:26.309 --> 00:37:29.278
I seeing cars where I ain't
never seen them before,
people I don't know.


00:37:29.412 --> 00:37:30.379
Yeah, me, too.


00:37:30.480 --> 00:37:31.242
EVA: Ho, ho, ho.


00:37:34.067 --> 00:37:35.261
Merry Christmas,
Charlie.


00:37:35.368 --> 00:37:36.460
Thank you.


00:37:36.569 --> 00:37:37.831
I love you.


00:37:38.004 --> 00:37:39.301
I love you, too.


00:37:40.807 --> 00:37:42.638
Here, take this.


00:37:42.909 --> 00:37:44.604
A quick toast,
and then I'll be off.


00:37:44.944 --> 00:37:47.276
<i>MAN ON TV:
What happened here
was an accident of war.</i>


00:37:47.447 --> 00:37:49.813
<i>Somebody made a mistake.</i>


00:37:50.817 --> 00:37:53.012
Bumpy ain't hardly
ever go out no more.


00:37:53.186 --> 00:37:55.416
After a certain point
he stayed in the house.


00:37:58.191 --> 00:38:00.352
Watch TV.


00:38:01.661 --> 00:38:03.629
Play chess.
Read the newspaper.


00:38:05.298 --> 00:38:07.391
I though he was just trying
to lead the quiet life,


00:38:07.500 --> 00:38:09.559
but no, he couldn't
go nowhere.


00:38:09.669 --> 00:38:11.136
Not without
something happening.


00:38:11.304 --> 00:38:12.794
Frankie...


00:38:12.972 --> 00:38:14.564
We can still go out.


00:38:14.741 --> 00:38:16.368
With who? Where?


00:38:16.476 --> 00:38:18.103
Well, with...


00:38:18.277 --> 00:38:19.869
But I know he's
under surveillance.


00:38:21.047 --> 00:38:22.708
Ain't gonna be
no Christmas time


00:38:22.882 --> 00:38:24.611
with my family
being here no more.


00:38:24.717 --> 00:38:27.845
Why don't you just pay
who you have to pay?


00:38:27.954 --> 00:38:30.047
I do pay them.
I pay thousands
and millions


00:38:30.223 --> 00:38:32.316
to dope dealers,
crooks, cops.


00:38:32.792 --> 00:38:33.850
I pay everybody.


00:38:34.026 --> 00:38:35.118
I pay more than
they should get.


00:38:35.228 --> 00:38:37.389
I can't satisfy
nobody!


00:38:37.497 --> 00:38:39.556
It's like dope!
Everybody's
strung out!


00:38:39.665 --> 00:38:41.690
The more you give 'em,
the more they want.


00:38:41.834 --> 00:38:44.132
They expect more.


00:38:45.138 --> 00:38:47.333
Give more and they want more.


00:38:52.044 --> 00:38:54.137
Do you want to go out?


00:38:55.081 --> 00:38:57.049
All right, baby.
Put something of
what you got.


00:38:57.150 --> 00:38:58.344
Should I?
Yeah.


00:38:58.451 --> 00:38:59.645
That's Christmas spirit.


00:38:59.752 --> 00:39:01.982
<i>That's what I'm talking about.
Feliz Navidad.</i>


00:39:02.088 --> 00:39:03.817
Something nice?
Mmm-hmm.


00:39:11.564 --> 00:39:12.895
We're going to
have a great time.


00:39:12.999 --> 00:39:14.091
<i>That's right, chica.</i>


00:39:14.200 --> 00:39:16.760
Mr. Lucas.
Enjoy your evening.


00:39:17.804 --> 00:39:19.362
It's all clear.


00:39:23.725 --> 00:39:24.453
WOMAN: (EXCITEDLY)
Nicky!


00:39:24.559 --> 00:39:26.356
NICKY: Who is that?
DOC: There's your boy,
Nicky. See him?


00:39:26.461 --> 00:39:27.450
NICKY: Know what I'm saying?


00:39:27.562 --> 00:39:30.156
Yeah, I see him.
Let's keep going.


00:39:30.899 --> 00:39:31.957
Around back?


00:39:32.067 --> 00:39:35.161
FRANK: Hell, no. I ain't
sneaking into my own club.


00:39:35.570 --> 00:39:37.504
Incredible.
Huh?


00:39:37.639 --> 00:39:39.834
(SPEAKING SPANISH)


00:39:59.761 --> 00:40:01.160
Come on.


00:40:04.032 --> 00:40:05.056
Hold on. Hold on.


00:40:05.200 --> 00:40:06.690
(CAR HONKING)


00:40:13.508 --> 00:40:14.532
What?


00:40:14.676 --> 00:40:16.473
I want to wait in the car.


00:40:16.578 --> 00:40:19.638
Frank, I got it. I got it.
I'll wait for it. I got it.


00:40:20.048 --> 00:40:22.073
Get that yellow sauce.
Yellow sauce.


00:40:22.217 --> 00:40:24.242
And the chicken.
The Kung Pao chicken.


00:40:30.525 --> 00:40:32.254
Can you turn the heater on?


00:40:38.600 --> 00:40:40.761
Shit. I'm gonna go
get the keys.


00:40:54.716 --> 00:40:57.241
Doc, give me the keys.
DOC: Here you go.


00:40:57.385 --> 00:40:58.943
(CAR ENGINE REVVING)


00:41:02.991 --> 00:41:04.253
Doc!


00:41:08.396 --> 00:41:10.193
Get out of the car.


00:41:16.638 --> 00:41:18.572
DOC: You okay?
Yeah.


00:41:18.673 --> 00:41:19.731
DOC: Shit.


00:41:19.841 --> 00:41:20.933
Come on.


00:41:21.076 --> 00:41:23.101
Come on, baby. You all right?


00:41:24.079 --> 00:41:25.376
Let's go.


00:41:46.034 --> 00:41:47.501
Was it Nicky?


00:41:49.171 --> 00:41:51.503
We'll go right now and
fucking kill him whether
it was him or not,


00:41:51.640 --> 00:41:53.574
you say the word, Frankie.


00:41:55.110 --> 00:41:57.442
We got to do something, Frank.


00:41:57.879 --> 00:41:58.903
We can't just sit here.


00:41:59.014 --> 00:42:00.504
We're leaving.


00:42:03.652 --> 00:42:05.313
All right, everybody get out.
TURNER: You all right, man?


00:42:05.453 --> 00:42:07.580
Go on home.
It's Christmas time.
Go and be with your families.


00:42:07.689 --> 00:42:08.986
I'm all right.


00:42:09.124 --> 00:42:12.025
Go on. Go ahead.
Be with your kids.


00:42:12.160 --> 00:42:13.457
Go ahead.


00:42:25.640 --> 00:42:26.698
Where are we gonna go, huh?


00:42:26.842 --> 00:42:28.434
We're gonna go to Spain,
somewhere? China?


00:42:28.543 --> 00:42:32.035
Huh? Come on, sit down.
Tell me where you want to go.


00:42:32.714 --> 00:42:35.649
Frank, we can go
anywhere we want.


00:42:35.750 --> 00:42:37.650
No, we can't.
We can live anywhere, Frank.


00:42:37.752 --> 00:42:39.447
Where? And do what?
Run? Hide?


00:42:39.554 --> 00:42:42.489
Frank Lucas don't run
from nobody, baby.


00:42:42.591 --> 00:42:44.388
We ain't going nowhere.
We're gonna stay right here.


00:42:44.526 --> 00:42:46.790
We're gonna stay right here.
This is my home.


00:42:46.895 --> 00:42:50.194
This is where my business is,
my wife, my mother, my family.


00:42:50.332 --> 00:42:52.800
My country.
I ain't going nowhere.


00:42:53.501 --> 00:42:55.696
I ain't running from nobody!


00:42:57.072 --> 00:42:58.699
This is America.


00:43:05.513 --> 00:43:08.073
And you ain't going
nowhere, either!


00:43:10.118 --> 00:43:11.244
Huh?


00:43:13.555 --> 00:43:16.217
<i>A ceasefire, internationally
supervised, will begin</i>


00:43:16.358 --> 00:43:20.658
<i>at 7:00 p.m. This Saturday,
January 27th, Washington time.</i>


00:43:20.762 --> 00:43:22.787
SPEARMAN: I'll call you back.


00:43:23.064 --> 00:43:25.294
Hey! What are you doing?


00:43:27.502 --> 00:43:28.696
Richie.


00:43:32.540 --> 00:43:33.632
Wow.


00:43:35.911 --> 00:43:40.712
So, what I hear it was
the Corsican mob took
a shot at Frank.


00:43:40.849 --> 00:43:42.680
You know, French Connection,
Fernando Rey,


00:43:42.784 --> 00:43:45.150
the exporters that
Frank has put out of business.


00:43:46.554 --> 00:43:48.681
Look, I can take care
of him in New York.


00:43:48.790 --> 00:43:50.257
I just don't want to have
to worry that every time


00:43:50.392 --> 00:43:51.859
he drives across
the bridge to Jersey,


00:43:51.960 --> 00:43:54.758
someone's gonna take
another shot at him.


00:43:54.896 --> 00:43:58.161
Richie, you and I gotta
start working together.


00:43:58.633 --> 00:44:00.999
We need to step up
our efforts.


00:44:01.369 --> 00:44:04.031
Next time,
their aim could be better.


00:44:04.639 --> 00:44:07.233
We need to keep
this cash cow alive.


00:44:13.081 --> 00:44:15.276
What the fuck
are you doing here?


00:44:15.784 --> 00:44:17.115
Whoa!


00:44:20.322 --> 00:44:24.258
Were you actually gonna
arrest Frank Lucas?
What's the matter with you?


00:44:24.659 --> 00:44:26.854
What, you don't know?
No.


00:44:27.562 --> 00:44:30.087
Everybody in
New Jersey's crazy.
Oh.


00:44:30.632 --> 00:44:34.068
You know what we do here?
Cops arrest bad guys.


00:44:36.304 --> 00:44:38.295
Before you get on
that bridge again,


00:44:38.440 --> 00:44:41.807
you should call me first,
just make sure it's safe.


00:44:45.013 --> 00:44:48.608
"I'm more enlightened
than some of my friends. I can
guarantee you peace of mind."


00:44:48.750 --> 00:44:51.048
That's what you
told me, Dominic.


00:44:51.152 --> 00:44:52.210
(BANGING ON TABLE)


00:44:52.320 --> 00:44:54.880
"I can guarantee you
peace of mind!"


00:44:54.990 --> 00:44:57.049
I don't feel so peaceful!


00:44:58.526 --> 00:44:59.652
Huh?


00:45:02.097 --> 00:45:04.292
They tried to kill my wife!


00:45:08.703 --> 00:45:10.261
Who was that? Huh?


00:45:12.474 --> 00:45:14.840
Maybe it was one
of your peoples.


00:45:14.976 --> 00:45:17.171
I don't know yet. No.
You don't know?


00:45:17.312 --> 00:45:18.836
You don't know.


00:45:20.215 --> 00:45:23.150
I'll tell you what I know.
Maybe I should just
put 500 guns


00:45:23.284 --> 00:45:25.343
out there on the street
and just start shooting up
some people,


00:45:25.453 --> 00:45:26.442
just to make a point.


00:45:26.554 --> 00:45:29.853
Frank, it was a junkie.
It was a rival.
Some dumb-ass kid


00:45:29.991 --> 00:45:33.688
trying to make a name
for himself. Somebody
you forgot to pay off.


00:45:33.828 --> 00:45:36.763
Someone you slighted
without even realizing it.


00:45:36.865 --> 00:45:41.131
Could be someone you
put out of business from being
so successful. Look at you.


00:45:41.970 --> 00:45:45.531
Success, it's got enemies,
Frank. Lots of enemies.


00:45:47.175 --> 00:45:49.700
So your success
took a shot at you. What are
you gonna do now?


00:45:49.844 --> 00:45:53.507
How you gonna kill it?
You're gonna become
unsuccessful?


00:45:54.482 --> 00:45:57.315
Frank, we can be successful
and have enemies, right?


00:45:57.719 --> 00:46:00.984
Or we can be unsuccessful,
too, you know,
we can have friends.


00:46:01.890 --> 00:46:03.983
That's the choice we make.


00:46:05.393 --> 00:46:09.022
<i>MAN ON TV: The final
evacuation of military
and diplomatic personnel</i>


00:46:09.164 --> 00:46:13.533
<i>continued throughout
the night, as North Vietnamese
troops marched on Saigon.</i>


00:46:13.868 --> 00:46:18.999
<i>The imminent fall of the city
has brought chaos and a
growing sense of desperation.</i>


00:46:19.107 --> 00:46:21.803
(PEOPLE CHEERING)


00:46:28.016 --> 00:46:31.417
International.


00:46:31.553 --> 00:46:33.077
<i>One moment, please.</i>


00:46:33.221 --> 00:46:34.813
(PHONE RINGING)


00:46:39.427 --> 00:46:41.361
(SPEAKING THAI)


00:46:41.463 --> 00:46:42.828
<i>FRANK: Yeah, Nate.</i>


00:46:42.931 --> 00:46:44.592
Hey, Frank. What's up, baby?


00:46:44.732 --> 00:46:46.097
What's going on over there?


00:46:46.201 --> 00:46:47.395
<i>It's all over.</i>


00:46:47.535 --> 00:46:49.366
Yeah, I'm watching the news.
What the hell's going on?


00:46:49.471 --> 00:46:51.166
<i>The game's over, Frank.</i>


00:46:51.272 --> 00:46:52.603
Huh?
It's done.


00:46:52.740 --> 00:46:54.708
Everybody going home, baby.
Give peace a chance.


00:46:54.809 --> 00:46:56.174
<i>Well, look, I'm not...
Listen to me.</i>


00:46:56.277 --> 00:46:57.835
I want two...


00:46:58.813 --> 00:47:01.611
(WHISPERING)
I want 2,000
keys in the air.


00:47:01.749 --> 00:47:05.014
<i>It's impossible, Frank.
All our resources are
going home. It's over.</i>


00:47:05.120 --> 00:47:06.883
I'll tell you what.
I'm on my way over there.


00:47:06.988 --> 00:47:08.922
<i>Right now? Oh, come...
Yeah.</i>


00:47:16.297 --> 00:47:18.458
